<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Botswana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Botswana is a landlocked country in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, much of it covered by the Kalahari Desert, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okavango-delta">Okavango Delta</a> in the north-west. Its Tswana chiefdoms came under British protection as the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in 1885, and it became independent in 1966 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seretse-khama">Seretse Khama</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaborone">Gaborone</a>. The discovery of diamonds soon after independence helped make it one of Africa's most stable and prosperous democracies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/botswana.jpg" alt="Botswana" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp, Gabbe, Madden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Botswana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
